            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0248" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/166</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1917-09-17T16:30:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1917-08-27T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 17, 1917, 4.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[For] Willard:</p>
                <p>Have heard nothing further from Lansing or you since your cables-August 17.
                    Commission to arrive Vladivostok September 28 and must then be advised of
                    situation and what you have decided as to our recommendations upon which the
                    movements of commission depend. There is a decided improvement efficiency
                    Siberian Railway already as a result of our work and expect much greater results
                    from our present trip with government officials. Answer quickly, care Consul at
                    Vladivostok.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
